{"extractor": "source-items/v1", "path": "/Users/rxw/Desktop/projects/research/claude-math-tcs-agent/plugins/math-tcs/examples/demo/source/01_unit-1-divisibility.md", "sha256": "ed191e2c602e59092a05ef88e6eacbb07ac6107241bb7950619535d6ca72fc8b", "slug": "dn", "slug_rule": "config", "chapter": "1", "chapter_rule": "explicit", "title": "Unit 1 — Divisibility", "items": [{"id": "dn-ch1-thm-1.1", "kind": "theorem", "label": "1.1", "section": "1.1", "page": 1, "lines": [11, 13], "statement": "If $a \\mid b$ and $b \\mid c$, then $a \\mid c$.", "proof": "Write $b = a q$ and $c = b r$. Then $c = (a q) r = a (q r)$, so $a \\mid c$. □", "excerpt_sha256": "7bef5946326f77b36b6cd6f10ce9838497a066f2dfb28eaef0914acb167aa140"}, {"id": "dn-ch1-thm-1.2", "kind": "theorem", "label": "1.2", "section": "1.1", "page": 1, "lines": [15, 17], "statement": "If $a \\mid b$ and $a \\mid c$, then $a \\mid (b + c)$.", "proof": "Write $b = a q$ and $c = a r$. Then $b + c = a q + a r = a (q + r)$. □", "excerpt_sha256": "bffe47e5a7cb7b9789b1de7a4c09e488b08a4782d2ef315a3a5725177f54db19"}, {"id": "dn-ch1-thm-1.3", "kind": "theorem", "label": "1.3", "section": "1.2", "page": 2, "lines": [23, 25], "statement": "If $a \\mid b$ and $a \\mid c$, then $a \\mid (b + b + c)$.", "proof": "By theorem 1.2, $a \\mid (b + c)$. Applying theorem 1.2 again to $b$ and $b + c$ gives $a \\mid (b + (b + c))$, which is the claim by associativity. □", "excerpt_sha256": "88a021d8ccf5eb5c93bf098e88c00b38c19bd5c0f9853014a5f1f67deecb6d8f"}, {"id": "dn-ch1-ex-1.2.1", "kind": "exercise", "label": "1.2.1", "section": "1.2", "page": 2, "lines": [29, 29], "statement": "Show that $a \\mid 0$ for every $a$.", "proof": null, "excerpt_sha256": "3cb0a7f5322332d08824a3f36be1397f509bac879789a16ff817ea5b6406052b"}, {"id": "dn-ch1-ex-1.2.2", "kind": "exercise", "label": "1.2.2", "section": "1.2", "page": 2, "lines": [31, 31], "statement": "Show that if $a \\mid b$ and $b \\mid a$ then $a = b$.", "proof": null, "excerpt_sha256": "6dd015c67577236b59ee58b4e55ca3d42d40de573b13a9b6f191704f36e20207"}], "counts": {"exercise": 2, "theorem": 3}, "path_relative": "../claude-math-tcs-agent/plugins/math-tcs/examples/demo/source/01_unit-1-divisibility.md"}
